# Task Tracker

A simple command-line Task Tracker built with Python.

This project was developed as part of the Task Tracker challenge from the Roadmap.sh beginners projects.
It allows users to create, manage, update, and persist tasks through a simple terminal interface while following an object-oriented design.

https://roadmap.sh/projects/task-tracker

## Features

* Create new tasks
* Update existing tasks
* Delete tasks
* Mark tasks as:

  * To Do
  * In Progress
  * Done

* Search tasks by ID
* List all tasks
* Filter tasks by status
* Save and load tasks automatically using JSON
* Basic unit tests with `unittest`

## Project Structure

```
task_tracker/
│
├── main.py          # Entry point
├── logics.py        # Core application logic
├── interface.py     # User interface
├── storage.py       # JSON persistence
├── task.py          # Task model
├── search.py        # Search utilities
├── test_main.py     # Unit tests
├── test_storage.py  # Unit tests
```

The project follows a simple separation of responsibilities:

* Interface handles user interaction.
* Logic manages application behavior.
* Storage is responsible for loading and saving data.

## Requirements

* Python 3.12 or later

No external libraries are required.

## How to Run

Clone the repository:

```bash
git clone https://github.com/your-username/task-tracker.git
```

Go to the project directory:

```bash
cd task_tracker
```

Run the application:

```bash
python main.py
```

## Running the Tests

Execute:

```bash
python -m unittest
```

or

```bash
python -m unittest discover
```

depending on your environment.


